<InfoPage title="Editorial Policy" kicker="How we publish" description="Standards for original SpicyBox comparisons, primary sources, updates, adult boundaries, and corrections."><h2>Useful before optimized</h2><p>Every page must answer a real reader question. Keywords belong in clear titles, headings, direct answers, and natural explanations—not repetition or hidden blocks.</p><h2>Primary sources</h2><p>Product claims link to official pages, Terms, and Privacy Policies where possible. We identify uncertainty and require live verification for changing templates, credits, plans, and controls.</p><h2>Adult and consent boundaries</h2><p>Coverage concerns adults. We enforce the published self-image-only rule in our guidance and never encourage non-consensual intimate imagery, real-person impersonation, or ambiguous-age content. We do not request credentials or personal images.</p><h2>Corrections</h2><p>Material changes update the visible revision date. Requests should identify the URL, disputed statement, and a direct source supporting the correction.</p></InfoPage>
